The harness under server/harness/ (and its fake agents under test/fixtures/)
was written for this project, with T3 Code (https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code,
read at commit 08b8689a) as reference: its Agent Client Protocol and Codex
app-server clients are where the message shapes we speak were learned, and its
orchestrator design is where the delegation and handoff rules come from. A few
small pieces follow its logic closely and say so where they are: the redaction
of an agent's stderr (server/harness/child.mjs, after
packages/provider-acp/src/server/stderr.ts), the rules of a portable context
handoff (server/harness/handoff.mjs, after
apps/server/src/orchestration-v2/ContextHandoffService.ts), the coalescing of
tool updates (server/harness/acp.mjs, after
packages/provider-acp/src/server/runtimeModel.ts), and the reading of Codex's
rate-limit windows (server/usage-sources.mjs, after
apps/server/src/provider/codexUsageLimits.ts). docs/HARNESS.md lists every
file consulted. T3 Code is distributed under the MIT licence:

